==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Uncertain. See {{w|Hoosier|Wikipedia's article on the subject}} for theories.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|/ˈhuʒɚ/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A native or resident of the American state of [[Indiana]].
# Someone associated with the {{w|Indiana University}}, for example as a student, alum, or sports team member, or as a fan.
# {{context|slang|St. Louis, Missouri|lang=en}} An [[uneducated]], [[tasteless]] [[Caucasian]] person.
#* '''2014''', Emily Giffin, ''The Emily Giffin Collection: Volume 2: Baby Proof'' (ISBN 1466882999)
#*: "The mall? Belinda, mall pickups are for '''hoosiers'''," I say, St. Louis slang for white trash. "With femullets." [...] "But Jake's no '''hoosier'''."
#* '''2015''', Pate McMichael, ''Klandestine: How a Klan Lawyer and a Checkbook Journalist ...'', page 2:
#*: Taken as a whole, the article portrayed Ray as an indigent, racist “'''Hoosier'''” (St. Louis slang for redneck) with an inept, habitual tendency to commit petty crimes.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|resident of Indiana}} [[Indianan]]
* {{sense|tasteless Caucasian}} [[white trash]]

